RAG Workshop – Environment Setup Guide

Please complete the following steps before beginning the RAG pipeline implementation.

1️⃣ Create a Google Colab Environment

Sign in to your Google account.

Navigate to: https://colab.research.google.com

Click “New Notebook” to create a fresh working environment.

This notebook will be used to build and execute the RAG pipeline.

2️⃣ Install Required Libraries

In the first cell of your notebook, install the necessary dependencies:

!pip install -q langchain langchain-community langchain-openai faiss-cpu langsmith

These libraries provide:

LangChain – RAG orchestration

FAISS – Vector database

OpenAI integration – LLM and embeddings

LangSmith – Prompt templates

Wait for installation to complete before proceeding.

3️⃣ Create an OpenRouter Account

Visit: https://openrouter.ai

Register for an account.

Navigate to the API Keys section.

Generate a new API key.

Securely copy and store your key (it begins with sk-or-...).

This key will be used to access language models and embedding services.

4️⃣ Add the OpenRouter API Key to Colab

To securely store your API key:

Click the 🔑 “Secrets” tab in the left sidebar of Colab.

Add a new secret:

Name: OPENROUTER_API_KEY

Value: Paste your API key.

Enable notebook access.

5️⃣ Read the API Key from Colab Secrets

In your notebook, retrieve and configure the API key:

from google.colab import userdata
import os

openrouter_key = userdata.get("OPENROUTER_API_KEY")
os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"] = openrouter_key

This securely loads your key into the environment for use by LangChain.

6️⃣ Test the Language Model (Mandatory Step)

Before building the RAG pipeline, confirm that the LLM connection works correctly.

from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI

llm = ChatOpenAI(
    model="openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    base_url="https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
    api_key=openrouter_key,
    temperature=0
)

print(llm.invoke("Say hello in one sentence.").content)

If a valid response is returned, the model is successfully connected.

7️⃣ Test the Embedding Model

Next, verify that embeddings are functioning correctly:

from langchain_openai import OpenAIEmbeddings

embeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings(
    model="openai/text-embedding-3-small",
    base_url="https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
    api_key=openrouter_key
)

vector = embeddings.embed_query("This is a test sentence.")
print("Embedding vector length:", len(vector))

You should see a numerical vector length (e.g., 1536), confirming that the embedding model is operational.